  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper evaluates portfolio optimization on three stocks (SPOT, META, MSFT) using historical YahooDataProvider data from 2021–2022 under constraints (risk factor 0.5, budget $500–$750, max 2 shares per company). Classical NumPyEigenSolver suggests buying SPOT and META, VQE suggests SPOT + 2×META + MSFT, while QAOA and the QAOA+VQE ensemble both recommend 1 share of each stock. The ensemble approach is claimed to have a higher probability of sampling the optimal portfolio but no quantitative runtime or resource metrics are reported.",
